 "kind": "statement",
 "title": "Etale morphisms are locally of finite presentation",
 "statement": "An etale morphism of schemes is locally of finite presentation; hence\nan etale morphism $U\\to X$ which is quasi-compact, with $X$ of\nfinite type over a field $K$, has $U$ of finite type over $K$.",
 "source": {
  "document": "literature/blueprint/master/blueprint/sec-smooth-purity/sk-prop-sf-kunneth-ordinary/lem-kun-etale-lfp.md",
  "place": "node lem-kun-etale-lfp, order 1705"
 },
 "stmt_deps": [],
 "proof": [
  {
   "text": "By [def-weil-pbc-scheme-conventions], étale means locally of\nfinite presentation, flat and unramified; with $X$ finite type over\n$K$ and $U\\to X$ quasi-compact, $U\\to K$ is quasi-compact and\nlocally of finite type, hence of finite type.",
   "uses": [
    "def-weil-pbc-scheme-conventions"
   ],
   "elementary": false
  }
 ],
